 "announcements": {
  "https://www.saudiexchange.sa/wps/portal/saudiexchange/newsandreports/issuer-news/issuer-announcements/issuer-announcements-details/?anId=98897&anCat=53&cs=8150&locale=en": {
   "text": "Element List Explanation\nIntroduction The Board of Directors of Allied Cooperative Insurance Group - ACIG is pleased to invite our valued shareholders to participate and vote in the Extraordinary General Assembly meeting, which includes the company's capital increase (the first meeting), scheduled to be held via modern technology using the Tadawulati system, God willing, on Wednesday, 15-06-1448 AH, corresponding to 25-11-2026 AD, at 7:00 PM.\nCity and Location of the Extraordinary General Assembly's Meeting The company's head office in Riyadh - through modern technology\nHyperlink of the Meeting Location Click Here\nDate of the General Assembly's Meeting 2026-11-25 Corresponding to 1448-06-15\nTime of the General Assembly’s Meeting 19:00\nMethodology of Convening the General Assembly’s Meeting Via modern technology means\nAttendance Eligibility, Registration Eligibility, and Voting End Shareholders who are registered in the issuers shareholders record at the Depositary Center by the end of the trade session prior to the general assembly meeting and in accordance with the laws and regulations. The shareholder has the right to delegate whomever other than the board of directors. The right to register a name to attend the general assembly meeting ends at the time of convening the general assembly meeting. The attendees right to vote on the items of the assembly’s agenda ends upon the end of screening the votes by the Screening Committee.\nQuorum for Convening the General Assembly's Meeting According to Article (33) of the company's Articles of Association, the quorum for holding an extraordinary General Assembly meeting for the bank is the presence of shareholders representing at least 50% of the capital. If the quorum is not completed at this meeting, a second meeting will be held one hour after the scheduled time of the first meeting, and the second meeting will be valid if attended by shareholders representing 25% of the capital.\nMeeting Agenda 1) Voting on the Board of Directors' recommendation to increase the company's capital by issuing 900,000 new ordinary shares with the suspension of pre-emptive rights as follows:\n• Method of increasing capital: increase the company's capital from SAR 291,000,000 divided into 29,100,000 equal ordinary shares, to SAR 300,000,000 divided into 30,000,000 equal ordinary shares with the suspension of pre-emptive rights, by issuing 900,000 new ordinary shares (representing approximately 3.09% of the company's current capital) with a nominal value of SAR 10 and an offering price of SAR 10 per share. Diyar Al-Arabiya Investment Company will subscribe to all the new shares, so its ownership will become 3% of the capital after the increase.\n• Total amount of capital increase: SAR 9,000,000\n• Capital before the increase: SAR 291,000,000\n• Capital after the increase: SAR 300,000,000\n• Number of shares before the increase: 29,100,000 shares\n• Number of shares after the increase: 30,000,000 shares\n• Percentage increase in capital: 3.09% of the current capital\n• Percentage decrease in current shareholders' ownership in the company due to the capital increase\n-Amendment of Article (7) of the company's Articles of Association related to capital. (Attached)\n- Amending Article (8) of the company's Articles of Association related to share subscription. (Attached).\n2) Voting on the Board of Directors' decision to appoint Mr. Rakan Nasr Abudef (Independent Member) to the Board, starting from his appointment date on 1 July 2026, to complete the Board's term until the end of the current term on 17 May 2029, replacing the former member Mr. Ali bin Yahya Al-Jaafari (Non-Executive Member). (Resume attached)\n3) Voting to authorize the Board of Directors with the powers of the General Assembly as stated in paragraph (1) of Article 27 of the Companies Law, for a period of one year from the date of the General Assembly's approval or until the end of the delegated Board of Directors' term, whichever comes first, according to the conditions set out in the executive regulations of the Companies Law for listed joint-stock companies.\nProxy Form \nThe shareholder right in discussing the assembly agenda topics, asking questions, and exercising the voting right Shareholders have the right to discuss the topics listed on the agenda of the assembly and ask questions, and registered shareholders in the Tadawulaty services can vote remotely on the meeting items through the Tadawulaty website at the link: (https://www.tadawulaty.com.sa) noting that registration on the Tadawulaty site and voting is free for all shareholders.\nDetails of the electronic voting on the Assembly’s agenda Esteemed shareholders can vote remotely on the agenda of the assembly through the electronic voting service, which will be available to registered shareholders on the Tadawulaty website starting from Saturday 11-06-1448 AH, corresponding to 21-11 -2026 at 1:00 AM, until the end of the assembly's meeting time. Registration and voting in Tadawulaty services will be available free of charge to all shareholders using the following link: www.tadawulaty.com.sa\nMethod of Communication in Case of Any Enquiries In case of any inquiries, please contact Mr. Muhannad Basilman\nphone number: 011-263 95 29,\nemail: m.basoliman@acig.com.sa\nAdditional Information It should be noted that Mr. Abdulilah Abdulaziz Rashid Al Huwaimel, the manager of Diyar Al-Arabiya Investment Company, which will subscribe for all the new shares, owns 1% of Masar Al Ruya International Trading Company, while members of the family of Mr. Yasser Mohammed Al Jarallah, the Company’s Vice Chairman, own the remaining 99% stake in Masar Al Ruya International Trading Company.\nIt should also be noted that Masar Al Ruya International Trading Company owns Private Tharawat Holding Company, which, in turn, owns a 15% stake in Allied Cooperative Insurance Group.\nAttached Documents   \nThe Capital Market Authority and Saudi Exchange take no responsibility for the contents of this disclosure, make no representations as to its accuracy or completeness, and expressly disclaim any liability whatsoever for any loss arising from, or incurred in reliance upon, any part of this disclosure, and the issuer accepts full responsibility for the accuracy of the information contained in it and confirms, having made all reasonable enquiries, that to the best of their knowledge and belief, there are no other facts or information the omission of which would make the disclosure misleading, incomplete or inaccurate.\nShare\nPrevious Announcements\nAllied Cooperative Insurance Group announces its Interim Financial Results for the period ending on 2026-09-30 ( Nine Months )\n8150\nACIG\n3.87 %\n1448/05/25     05/11/2026 08:51:41\nBoard of directors of the Allied Cooperative Insurance Group invites its shareholders to attend the extraordinary general assembly meeting which includes the increase of the company's capital (the first meeting) via modern technology.\n8150\nACIG\n3.87 %\n1448/05/22     02/11/2026 08:51:46\nAllied Cooperative Insurance Group (ACIG) announce receiving the decision from the Insurance Authority to stop the company from issuing comprehensive motor insurance policies while continuing to renew existing policies\n8150\nACIG\n3.87 %\n1448/04/16     27/09/2026 08:04:25\nView all announcements\nCompany Performance\nACIG\nAdd To Watchlist\nZoom\n1D\n1M\n3M\n1Y\n3Y\n5Y\nInception\n10:00\n12:00\n14:00\n6\n5.5\n5.75\n6.25\nZoom ▾\nNov 25, 2026\n→\nNov 25, 2026\nKey Parameters\nLast Price\n5.9\nNet Change\n0.22 (+3.87%)\nValue Traded (Sar)\n6,300,489.81\nVolume Traded\n1,076,541\nSee The Company Profile"
  }
